    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89f8b940c019fc9539fbf76a5": {
      "title": "Federal Work Study: Student Employee Academic Support Specialist",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Federal Work Study: Student Employee Academic Support Specialist Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 215 # of Openings: 0 Student Employee:  Academic Operations Support Specialist Position Overview The Academic Operations Support Specialist Assistant Provost for Academic Operations in managing the daily operations of the Academics Office. This Howell campus, in-person position (not virtual or hybrid) involves a variety of tasks aimed at ensuring the smooth functioning of the department, including data management, report generation, and office organization. The role provides an opportunity for students to gain hands-on experience in academic administration and operations within a higher education setting. Responsibilities Data Management Enter and update data into various databases and systems accurately. Verify and reconcile data to ensure its accuracy and completeness. Generate reports and summaries to assist with departmental data analysis. Office Operations Assist in maintaining organization and order within the Academics Office. Handle phone, e-mail, and walk-in inquiries, providing timely and professional responses. Revise, create, and manage handouts, flyers, website language, etc. to support communication with students, faculty, and staff on behalf of Academics. Expected Skills Complete special projects and initiatives as assigned by the Provost, Assistant Provost for Academic Operations, Deans, or Instructional Designer. Participate in meetings and contribute to discussions on process improvements. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion. Proficiency in both Google Apps and Microsoft Office Suite (i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to multitask and prioritize tasks effectively. Previous office or administrative experience is a plus but not required. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current student at Cleary University. At least 2 semesters remaining in your academic program. Must be in good academic standing (and continue to be in good academic standing). Demonstrated interest in working in the higher education setting in academic affairs/operations. Can commit to working physically on the Howell campus 10-15 hours per week during the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 Semesters. Application Process Interested applicants should submit: Updated Resume. Cover letter highlighting interest in position and career goals. Relevant projects or coursework. (Not required, but recommended) Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a091ca94fb0c69": {
      "title": "Student Academic Services Specialist",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Academic Services Specialist Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 224 # of Openings: 1 Student Academic Services Specialist Department: Academic Affairs and Services Reports To: Director of Student Academic Services Employment Classification: Full Time/Exempt Location: Howell Position Summary: Pr ovides frontline service for a cohort of students and operational support to the Student Academic Services department. The Specialist is responsible for processing academic records transactions, supporting course registration and scheduling, and providing high-quality service to students, faculty, and staff through the central ticketing system, phone, email, and in-person interactions. This position plays a vital role in ensuring the accuracy of student records, timely resolution of student requests, and seamless integration of advising and registrar functions. The Specialist acts as a bridge between compliance-driven processes and student-facing support, contributing directly to institutional risk reduction and student success outcomes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Student Records & Compliance Support • Advise students to navigate key transactions including withdrawals, drops, and program change requests. • Support transcript evaluations, degree audits, and graduation processes. • Assist with SAP (Satisfactory Academic Progress) notifications, compliance documentation, and FERPA-protected record management. • Maintain accurate records in the Student Information System (SIS) and ensure consistency across advising notes and records. Scheduling & Operations • Provide administrative support to the Dean for semester course scheduling and section building. • Ensure accuracy of student academic plans. • Assist students with schedule-related questions and data entry. Student Success & Advising Support • Respond to student inquiries via phone, email, walk-ins, and the ticketing system, escalating complex issues to the Director as needed. • Support proactive outreach campaigns (e.g., registration reminders, retention interventions). • Provide frontline assistance to students during high-volume periods such as registration, add/drop, and commencement. Service Excellence • Serve as the first point of contact for Student Academic Services, triaging requests efficiently. • Contribute to a culture of student-centered service with professionalism, empathy, and accountability. • Ensure timely resolution of tickets and maintain accurate documentation of all student interactions. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree. • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. • Demonstrated ability to handle confidential student information in compliance with FERPA. • Excellent written and verbal communication skills. • Proficiency with student information systems and Microsoft Office Suite. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience working with course scheduling or degree audit systems. • Familiarity with CRM or ticketing systems for student service management. • Knowledge of academic policy, student success practices, and compliance standards. Key Attributes and Competencies: • Student-centered approach to service delivery. • Ability to balance multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. • Collaborative mindset with cross-functional teams. • Problem-solving skills with a focus on timely and accurate resolution. • Commitment to supporting a diverse student population. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: • Ability to lift up to 10 pounds. • Regularly required to stand, walk, sit, talk, and hear. • Attendance at special events required, which may be in the evenings/weekends . Compensation and Benefits: Salary commensurate with experience. Eligible for full-time university benefits package. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome and encourage applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78859f9eb34c34019ec77535991ad9": {
      "title": "Director of the Center for Public Safety Education & Associate Professor",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Director of the Center for Public Safety Education & Associate Professor Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 209 # of Openings: 0 Director of the Center for Public Safety Education & Associate Professor About the Opportunity Cleary University is seeking an innovative and student-centered academic leader to serve as the inaugural Director of the Center for Public Safety Education on our teaching and learning team of full-time faculty. This position supports Cleary’s educational programs serving public safety professionals, including accelerated degree completion programs and noncredit professional development. The Director provides academic leadership for these programs including meeting with public safety leaders and prospective students on how the programs support professional and career goals both within public safety and beyond. As a full-time faculty member, this individual will support curriculum quality, faculty development, experiential learning, and workforce readiness within designated academic domain(s). This includes contributing to AI implementation efforts, supporting adjunct faculty success, contributing to curriculum development and assessment, and helping ensure students graduate with the applied professional skills of The Cleary Mind TM . The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to experiential education, workforce alignment, and the thoughtful integration of artificial intelligence into higher education. This role will collaborate closely with academic leadership including the Chief Academic Officer, Deans, other members of the faculty team, student support services, members of adjunct faculty, and instructional design to support instructional quality, student engagement, and continuous improvement across programs within the assigned domain(s). This role also carries faculty rank as an Associate Professor at Cleary University, combining academic leadership responsibilities with active teaching and student engagement. The successful candidate will contribute to instruction, curriculum development, assessment, and academic governance while serving as a leader within their assigned academic domain(s). Cleary University values faculty leaders who remain closely connected to the student experience, instructional innovation, and the practical application of workforce-relevant education. Reports To: Dean of Graduate Studies and Adult Programs What You’ll Do: Serve as the academic lead and subject matter expert for one or more of the following domains based on experience and qualifications. Leadership Human Resource Management Business Communications Digital Marketing Project Management Cybersecurity Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses within qualified disciplines and levels using applied, student-centered teaching methodologies, in multiple modalities (in person, hybrid, asynchronous). Support and mentor adjunct faculty through onboarding, coaching, professional development, instructional guidance, and ongoing collaboration. Contribute to the implementation of AI initiatives across the university and support the discipline-specific integration of AI within assigned academic areas. Collaborate with academic leadership on curriculum development, assessment, accreditation readiness, and program review initiatives. Promote experiential and workforce-aligned learning practices that emphasize practical application of the domain and The Cleary Mind TM professional attributes. Assist in ensuring instructional consistency, academic quality, and positive student learning experiences across modalities and student populations. Participate in institutional committees, strategic initiatives, and professional development activities. Contribute to student recruitment, retention, and engagement initiatives. Pursue available funding for initiatives of the Center for Public Safety Education. What We’re Looking For: Earned master’s degree from an institutionally accredited college or university in a relevant discipline. Doctorate or active doctoral enrollment preferred. 10+ years of relevant industry experience within public safety. Knowledge of the current application of AI in one or more of the domain areas listed in this job description. Experience with emerging technologies, including AI, and their impact on teaching and learning and industry use within the individual’s domain areas. Teaching experience in higher education, training, or professional development environments. Demonstrated ability to mentor, coach, or support teams in academic or professional environments. Familiarity with instructional technologies and learning management systems in multiple delivery modalities. Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Commitment to student success and workforce-ready education. Experience with curriculum development, assessment, or accreditation processes. What Makes a Strong Candidate: A strong candidate is deeply committed to the student experience and believes that higher education should be transformational, engaging, and genuinely valuable to students’ professional futures. They are energized by the opportunity to help students develop not only technical and disciplinary knowledge, but also the confidence, adaptability, and professional skills necessary to thrive in a rapidly evolving workforce. The ideal candidate is excited about the future of teaching and learning, particularly the thoughtful integration of artificial intelligence into education and professional practice within their domain. They are intellectually curious, forward-thinking, and committed to remaining current as both an educator and an industry expert. They actively monitor emerging trends, technologies, and practices and are eager to translate those developments into meaningful, applied learning experience for students. Strong candidates are passionate advocates for high-quality, applied professional education that connects classroom learning to real-world outcomes. They understand the importance of preparing graduates who are workforce ready and professionally capable. They value and champion the importance of The Cleary Mind TM professional skills and intentionally embed them throughout the student learning experience. Successful candidates thrive in collaborative academic environments and are excited to contribute to a highly innovative and student-focused teaching and learning culture. They are energized by the opportunity to help shape modern educational experiences in creative, ambitious, and impactful ways alongside a team committed to continuous improvement and innovation. They also recognize that student-centered education requires meaningful engagement, responsiveness, mentorship, and support. Strong candidates are approachable, relationship-oriented educators who are willing to inest in students as individuals and help create an environment where students feel challenged, supported, and connected – no matter the course modality. Finally, strong candidates are enthusiastic about supporting and mentoring adjunct faculty. They can coach, encourage, and inspire Cleary University’s talented team of adjunct faculty members fostering a shared commitment to excellence. Location and Schedule: This position is based on-site at Cleary University’s campus in Howell, Michigan. Regular on-site presence is required. Travel will be required both within Michigan and out-of-state. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required according to your course schedule, which varies each semester, and for occasional campus and community events. This is a year-round faculty position with teaching requirements throughout the entire year. Compensation : Salary commensurate with experience. Cleary offers a competitive benefits package including health coverage, retirement contributions, and tuition benefits. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
