      "title": "Part-Time Educator (Graduate Programs)",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Part-Time Educator (Graduate Programs) Location: Remote Job Id: 105 # of Openings: 9999 Part Time Educator (Graduate Program) DESCRIPTION | QUALIFICATIONS: Cleary University seeks passionate and student-centered instructors who are highly engaging and intrinsically motivated to create meaningful, transformational, and dynamic learning experiences in the online learning environment. We need creative, innovative, and adaptable instructors who understand the level of technical engagement, personal investment, and technology-integrated approach needed to connect with our graduate students in the online learning environment. Cleary is specifically looking for professionals who are tech savvy, possesses a high-level of self-assuredness, and are dedicated to playing a critical role in the personal and professional growth of students. We are currently seeking professionals with terminal (Doctorate, DEd, EdD, MFA, PhD, JD, DBA) degrees in the following disciplines: Analytics & Statistics Accounting & Finance Philosophy Business & Management Communication Economics Marketing Human Resource Management Leadership Organizational Development Education DUTIES | RESPONSIBILITIES Teaching : Utilize Canvas (LMS) engagement tools and video, digital communication, and content development features to deliver course content and maintain and record classroom attendance, grades, and assignments according to institutional standards Personally connect with students via video, voice, or in-person weekly Direct active, online classroom activities with students Utilize group work and online collaboration techniques to build student relationships and belonging Practice interactive pedagogical techniques to engage students and enhance the student experience in the online classroom Utilize the online calendar to regularly schedule office hours (minimum of 1 hour per week for each 3 credit hour course) and / or be available online to students on a regular basis Actively engage students in dialog and communication to form connections and build positive, lasting student/faculty/University relationships Assess student learning based on institutional outcomes, course goals and objectives in an unbiased, timely, and respectful manner Implement relevant, creative, and effective teaching methodologies to engage learners and inspire original thinking, problem solving, and entrepreneurial mindset Present course content through the filters of global sustainability, environment, AI/IT, communications, and ethics PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT |PROFESSIONALISM : Interact with student groups, campus administration, and faculty peers on regular basis Aspire to maintain a professional growth mindset and frequently seek opportunities to build scholarly and academic credentials, certifications, and experiences Purposely seek knowledge and practice in current and meaningful student engagement techniques, classroom management, student coaching, and evolving academic/learning needs and expectations . The ideal candidate is a people-centered and engaging professional who: Continuously seeks opportunity for personal and professional growth Applies expertise and professional knowledge to course content Utilizes digital technology, video, podcasts, and multimedia to communicate with online graduate students Utilizes digital technology, video, podcasts, and multimedia to enhance content and material and create active learning activities for online graduate students Utilizes student-centered and active learning techniques to build long-lasting skill sets Is intrinsically motivated to personally connect with professional distance students Is highly engaging in technical and in-person environments Enjoys working collaboratively with other faculty members, departments, and staff to develop a meaningful experience for graduate students Possesses natural people and communication skills Creatively implements methodology and activities that promote critical thinking, problem solving, and creativity Is enthusiastic about education for diverse, entrepreneurial-minded, global, multi-cultural graduate students Required Qualifications : Able to communicate with students on a daily basis Create custom videos, podcasts, or other media on a weekly basis Provide additional resources and content knowledge on a weekly basis Digital communication skills and can utilize instructional technologies Highly engaging and passionate about education Out of the box, innovative, creative thinking skills Natural people and communication skills Minimum of a terminal degree (Doctorate, DEd, EdD, MFA, PhD, JD, DBA)  in the appropriate field is required **CMA or CPA preferred for accounting Prior teaching experience is preferred Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
