    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0ed3a990a7ffe": {
      "title": "Enrollment Coordinator",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Enrollment Coordinator Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 227 # of Openings: 0 Enrollment Coordinator About the Role Cleary University is seeking a highly organized, student-focused Enrollment Coordinator to serve as a key member of the Enrollment Management team. This role is often the first impression of the University — the person who helps students and families navigate important decisions with clarity, confidence, and care. As the primary point of contact for prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, the Enrollment Coordinator delivers timely, accurate, and solutions-oriented guidance related to admissions, enrollment, financial aid, scholarships, and university policies. If you enjoy solving problems, supporting students, and making complex processes feel manageable, this role offers meaningful daily impact. Beyond frontline service, this position plays an integral operational leadership role within Enrollment Management. The Enrollment Coordinator oversees the Student Ambassador Program and student workers, manages casework in Salesforce, coordinates campus tours and recruitment events, and collaborates across departments to ensure a seamless student experience. This is an ideal opportunity for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, values both structure and service, and wants to grow within higher education administration while contributing to a mission-driven institution. Key Responsibilities Frontline Student Support Serve as a primary point of contact via phone, email, chat, Microsoft Teams, and in-person interactions. Provide accurate information regarding admissions processes, registration, financial aid basics, scholarships, deadlines, and university policies. Manage, document, and resolve student cases in Salesforce with prompt follow-up and detailed recordkeeping. Research and troubleshoot enrollment-related issues across multiple systems; escalate complex matters appropriately. Oversee day-to-day front desk operations to ensure a welcoming and efficient environment. Supervise student workers, including hiring, training, scheduling, task delegation, and performance feedback. Manage the Student Ambassador Program, including recruitment, onboarding, communications, assignments, and accountability. Coordinate campus tour staffing and admissions event coverage. Assist Admissions Counselors with recruitment logistics, travel coordination, outreach, and communication workflows. Plan and support recruitment events including open houses, campus tours, interview days, Cleary Days, virtual sessions, and yield events. Conduct outreach to newly enrolled first-year students to support onboarding and retention efforts. Serve as a liaison between prospective students and admissions representatives. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree required (business-related field preferred). Experience in enrollment, admissions, financial aid, customer service, or student services preferred. Familiarity with Salesforce, ZoomInfo, Microsoft Office Suite, and Microsoft Teams. Strong attention to detail and ability to manage high-volume tasks under deadlines. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Ability to multitask and prioritize in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Key Attributes Student-centered mindset with empathy and service excellence. Strong organizational and operational skills. Professional discretion and ability to manage sensitive information. Adaptability and flexibility in evolving environments. Working Conditions Standard office environment with frequent student and staff interaction. Ability to lift up to 10 pounds. Regular use of computer-based systems. Occasional evening and weekend work required during peak enrollment periods. Why Join Cleary? At Cleary University, we believe education should be personal, practical, and transformational. Our team members play a direct role in helping students achieve meaningful career outcomes and life-changing opportunities. As part of Enrollment Management, you will be at the center of that mission — guiding students through one of the most important decisions of their lives. Cleary offers a collaborative, team-oriented culture where innovation and continuous improvement are encouraged. Employees have opportunities to grow professionally, contribute ideas that shape processes, and make a visible impact across campus. With a strong commitment to student success, employee development, and community engagement, Cleary provides an environment where your work truly matters. In addition to competitive compensation, full-time employees enjoy a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, and vision coverage, disability insurance, tuition grants, paid professional development, paid personal days, and more. Compensation & Benefits Salary commensurate with experience. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89f8b940c019fc96881a67f80": {
      "title": "Student Worker: Admissions",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker: Admissions Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 216 # of Openings: 0 Student Worker: Clerical Assistant General Description The team of student workers provides support to run the daily operations of the Admissions Office. The primary way in which they offer support is by providing event support when guests attend recruitment events on campus. The student worker also provides secondary support to the main Admissions Office where guests check in for their campus visits. Lastly, student workers occasionally provide support by entering all prospective student data into the campus database for Admissions Staff to use during the recruitment process. Specific Responsibilities 85% Event and Campus Visit Support Greet and register visitors, and issue any required identification badges, parking information, and visit schedule. Prepare for tours by putting together tour items such as draw string bags, and program folders. Escort individuals or groups around campus, on campus tours, or through places of interest. Provide directions and other pertinent information to visitors. Distribute brochures, program information, and explain admission and registration processes and operations. Support admissions office with on-campus events. Be service orientated by actively looking for ways to help staff and visitors. Operate campus telephone line to answer, screen, or forward calls, this includes: providing information, taking messages, or scheduling appointments. 10% Front Office Support Greet visitors entering the office, determine nature and purpose of visit, and direct or escort the visitors to specific destinations. Provide information about establishment, such as location of departments or offices, employees within the organization, or services provided. Collect, sort, distribute, or prepare mail, messages, or courier deliveries. Maintain storage areas Perform the process of opening and closing the office when needed 5% Data Entry Receive, verify, and process all pieces of the application file, including but not limited to the application for admission, character recommendation, high school transcript, college transcript, and ACT/SAT score in database. Receive, verify, and process all prospective student inquires. Enter prospective student data from info cards obtained through various on and off campus events. Load batch lists into database. Execute all of Admissions data entry, daily and event based recruitment mailings, and daily recruitment correspondence including daily tracker actions. Create/edit all student records in the database for both candidates and applicants, ensuring complete biographical and mailing data in each student record. Present completed applicant files to the Admissions Counselor for review and acceptance Receive, verify, and process all pieces submitted by accepted applicants, including but not limited to the immunization forms and final high school transcripts At all times and in all situations, represent CU and the Admissions Department in a professional and friendly manner Minimum Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent is required. Experience in an office setting preferred. Must be a current student at Cleary University and be in good standing with the university. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to relate well with different people in a variety of situations Excellent communication skills Ability to communicate effectively with other offices on campus Thoroughly understands the admissions strategy and procedures Ability to use computers and basic programs (campus database, e-mail, Microsoft Office, internet etc.) Ability to be self-motivated and self-managed to meet deadlines Ability to plan and execute duties with attention to detail Ability to problem-solve and make reasoned decisions Be able to meet deadlines, be flexible, and most of all be team-oriented Knowledgeable about basic university policies in the areas of housing, financial aid, parking, and academic programs Ability to work independently and adapt to a variety of roles and environments Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with multiple demands Ability to work with a team of admissions personnel in an office setting Have critical thinking ability by using logic and reasoning to identify the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions, conclusions or approaches to problems. Providing information to supervisors, co-workers, and other admissions staff by telephone, in written form, email, or in person. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a1983930e90198568730ec5efd": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach (General/Future Interest)",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Assistant Coach (General/Future Interest) Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 131 # of Openings: 0 ATHLETIC ASSISTANT COACH JOB SUMMARY: The Assistant Coach will support the daily operations of the Cleary University Athletic Department. The Assistant Coach will aid the Head Coach in team management, training, recruitment, and academic oversight, while contributing to the success and integrity of Cleary's NAIA athletics. JOB DUTIES: Assist in planning and conducting practices, workouts, and competitions. Support the Head Coach in implementing strategic game plans and performance improvement. Aid in the identification and recruitment of prospective student-athletes who align with Cleary’s academic and athletic standards. Promote and monitor the academic success of student-athletes, encouraging use of Cleary support resources (e.g., study tables, tutoring). Help coordinate team travel, logistics, and equipment management. Represent Cleary Athletics in a professional and sportsmanlike manner on and off the field. Engage in departmental fundraising, community outreach, and athletic promotional activities. Ensure compliance with NAIA, WHAC Conference, and Cleary University rules and policies. Serve as a positive mentor, modeling integrity, accountability, and leadership. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Prior coaching experience at the collegiate, club, or high school level preferred. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work flexible hours including evenings, weekends, and travel. CPR/AED certification or willingness to obtain upon hiring. Valid driver’s license and ability to be cleared to drive university vehicles. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89e235a1d019e40558c341455": {
      "title": "Athletic Dept Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Athletic Dept Graduate Assistant Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 195 # of Openings: 0 ATHLETICS DEPARTMENT GRADUATE ASSISTANT JOB SUMMARY: The Athletic Department Graduate Assistant will assist the athletic department administration with the daily operational tasks.  The Graduate Assistant will be involved in every aspect of the athletic department, including, but not limited to, compliance, facility management, sports information, marketing, game operations, business aspects and other areas assigned by the athletic administration. JOB DUTIES: Responsible for assisting in the planning, directing, and evaluating all aspects and facets of a successful program at the NAIA level. Supporting the Assistant Athletic Director with all aspects of NAIA compliance. Assisting the Athletic Department Business Coordinator with daily tasks as needed. Aiding the Sports Information Director with taking stats, preparing news releases and feature articles for the Cougars Website, and documenting special athletic events. Coordinate set up, take down and supervision of all intercollegiate events. Reach out to visiting teams prior to competition and inform them of our event plan and details such as athletic trainer services, event location, protocols, locker room availability, parking, etc. Act as liaison for all visiting teams, and serve as game day host Facilitating athletic department community service and fundraising events. Provide game updates and promote Cleary University through various social media platforms. Providing support to all coaches when necessary. Oversee administrative processes and procedures as assigned. Serve as a leader, mentor, and role-model to the student-athletes of the athletic department. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required and be accepted into the Cleary University graduate program. Candidate must be enrolled in at least one graduate class per session (three credits) and remain in good academic standing (3.0 or higher GPA). The Graduate Assistant will receive a 75% graduate tuition scholarship provided the above standard and requirements are met. Previous experience as a student-athlete or employment within a collegiate athletic department. Ability to frequently work weekends and nights. Strong organizational skills with an ability to effectively multi-task are essential. Excellent oral and written communication skills, computer literacy and strong interpersonal skills to work with various college constituencies. The ability to work a flexible and irregular schedule. Works well as a team member or independently. Excels in prioritizing multiple tasks with attention to detail, problem solving and follow-through to consistently meet expectations and deadlines. Ability to work with students and diverse constituencies. A positive attitude and an understanding of the importance of being open-minded and flexible. Travel is necessary with a valid driver’s license required. Ability to successfully pass a background check also required. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887ac9efb876c019f41b65db51753": {
      "title": "Federal Work Study: Athletics Student Worker",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Federal Work Study: Athletics Student Worker Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 213 # of Openings: 0 ATHLETIC DEPARTMENT STUDENT EMPLOYEE JOB SUMMARY: The Student Employee will support the daily operations of the Cleary University Athletic Department. This role provides hands-on experience in athletics administration, game day operations, marketing, and office management while promoting a positive environment for Cleary University Athletics. JOB DUTIES: Set up and break down athletic facilities for home events such as placing signage, setting up scorer’s table and arranging chairs and benches Operate the scoreboard, shot clock and game clock for sports such as hockey, soccer, baseball and softball Serve as a public address announcer when needed Ensure officials and visiting teams have required accommodations Capture in-game photos or videos for marketing and social media Assist with livestream broadcasts, including camera operation Serve as front desk attendant and answer phone calls and greet visitors Monitor Wellness Center and weight room after hours and responsible for securing the building Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Current Cleary University in good academic standing Interest in sports management, event operations, sports communications or related fields Excellent communication and teamwork skills Ability to work evenings, weekends, and flexible hours based on event schedules Proficient in Microsoft Word and Excel Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
