    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89e235a1d019e40522a00132e": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Sport",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Graduate Assistant - Sport Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 194 # of Openings: 0 GRADUATE ASSISTANT - SPORT JOB SUMMARY: The Graduate Assistant will serve as an assistant coach with the designated Cleary University athletic team as well as take on additional duties within the designated sport’s office and the Athletic Department, including, but not limited to: assisting with the recruiting, the management of academic success programs, game day operations, scheduling of practices and conditioning, as well as participating and managing fundraising efforts and coaching assignments during practices and games. JOB DUTIES: Responsible for assisting in the planning, directing, and evaluating all aspects and facets of a successful program at the NAIA level. Assist in the creation and distribution of practice plans. Will serve as an assistant coach during practices and games, primarily for the Cleary varsity program, but also the Junior Varsity program when needed. Managing the recruiting database, following up with admissions and financial aid regularly on top prospects, arranging individual visits, being the primary person during campus-wide Visit Days and following up with incoming students in regard to any needed documentation, including Sports Medicine forms, registration, housing, and NAIA Eligibility Center. Manage class schedules each semester and conduct weekly study tables throughout the semester. Will be the point person, as needed, on home game days for visiting teams. Providing support to all coaches when necessary. Oversee administrative processes and procedures as assigned. Serve as a leader, mentor, and role-model to the student-athletes of the athletic department. Contribute to maintaining the Athletic Department website and social media platforms, along with marketing of the Cleary University Athletic Department. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required and be accepted into the Cleary University graduate program. Candidate must be enrolled in at least one graduate class per session (three credits) and remain in good academic standing (3.0 or higher GPA). The Graduate Assistant will receive a graduate tuition scholarship provided the above standard and requirements are met. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89e235a1d019e40590a9c158c": {
      "title": "Sports Information Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Sports Information Graduate Assistant Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 196 # of Openings: 0 SPORTS INFORMATION GRADUATE ASSISTANT JOB SUMMARY: The Athletic Department Graduate Assistant will assist the athletic department administration with the daily operational tasks.  The Graduate Assistant will be involved in every aspect of the athletic department, including, but not limited to, compliance, facility management, sports information, marketing, game operations, business aspects and other areas assigned by the athletic administration. JOB DUTIES: Responsible for assisting in the planning, directing, and evaluating all aspects and facets of a successful program at the NAIA level. Aiding the Sports Information Director with taking stats, preparing news releases and feature articles for the Cougars Website, and documenting special athletic events. Facilitating athletic department community service and fundraising events. Providing support to all coaches when necessary. Oversee administrative processes and procedures as assigned. Serve as a leader, mentor, and role-model to the student-athletes of the athletic department. Contribute to maintaining the Athletic Department website and social media platforms, along with marketing of the Cleary University Athletic Department. Ensure accurate stats at assigned home contests and oversee quick delivery of stats to opposing teams. Ensure excellent, timely, and accurate information on electronic and printed material that pertains to the athletic department. Write and edit game summaries for some athletic events. Provide game updates and promote Cleary University through various social media platforms. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required and be accepted into the Cleary University graduate program. Candidate must be enrolled in at least one graduate class per session (three credits) and remain in good academic standing (3.0 or higher GPA). The Graduate Assistant will receive a 75% graduate tuition scholarship provided the above standard and requirements are met. Previous experience as a student-athlete or employment within a collegiate athletic department. Ability to frequently work weekends and nights, totaling 15-20 hours a week. Strong organizational skills with an ability to effectively multi-task are essential. Excellent oral and written communication skills, computer literacy and strong interpersonal skills to work with various college constituencies. The ability to work a flexible and irregular schedule. Works well as a team member or independently. Excels in prioritizing multiple tasks with attention to detail, problem solving and follow-through to consistently meet expectations and deadlines. Ability to work with students and diverse constituencies. A positive attitude and an understanding of the importance of being open-minded and flexible. Travel is necessary with a valid driver’s license required. Ability to successfully pass a background check also required. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a8a0abfd5001a0d96b4d4e1a57": {
      "title": "Controller",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Controller Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 226 # of Openings: 0 Controller Cleary University is seeking an experienced, hands-on Controller to lead our accounting operations and provide day-to-day financial leadership for the Finance Department and Business Office. Reporting to the CFO, you'll own the integrity of our accounting records, financial reporting, budget maintenance, internal controls, reconciliations, audit preparation, and cash management, while directly supervising the Business Office. This role combines strong technical accounting skills with people management: you'll improve processes, build accountability, and personally engage in critical accounting work when needed. What you'll do: Direct the accounting function and lead monthly/annual close in accordance with GAAP Lead and supervise the Business Office (AP, AR, student accounts, collections, cash receipts) Maintain a rolling cash-flow forecast and oversee bank reconciliations Serve as primary coordinator for the annual financial statement audit and Single Audit Oversee federal Title IV financial-aid accounting and reconciliation Manage the operational side of the annual budgeting process Lead Finance's use of Jenzabar One and drive process improvement Partner across CFO, President, Financial Aid, HR, Enrollment, and Advancement Minimum qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business, or related field 7+ years of progressively responsible accounting/financial-management experience Strong GAAP knowledge and experience supervising accounting staff Advanced Excel and financial-systems proficiency Preferred qualifications: CPA strongly preferred Higher education or nonprofit accounting experience strongly preferred Experience with federal grants, Title IV aid, or Single Audit Experience with Jenzabar or another higher-ed ERP Working conditions: On-site at Cleary's Howell campus, with some hybrid flexibility possible after onboarding. Periodic evening/weekend work during audit, close, and budget cycles. About Cleary University: A private, nonprofit university founded in 1883, focused on practical, career-focused education and entrepreneurship, serving students from its Howell campus and Detroit presence. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78839fa064212401a0690778775454": {
      "title": "Prep Cook",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Prep Cook Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 223 # of Openings: 0 Cook SUMMARY OF BASIC JOB FUNCTION: The Cleary University Prep Cook (afternoons/early evening shift) role will involve performing meal-prep activities, ensuring food plating is visually appealing, and maintaining cleanliness in your station. You will also work as a team with others to ensure a clean and quality buffet. Replace low or empty containers on the buffet with clean containers full of fresh products. Serve food at proper temperatures. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: You must be at least 18 years of age to be considered for this role. Proven ability to read and understand recipes. Demonstrates passion and enthusiasm for working in the kitchen. Actively represents the Cleary University to students. Proven knowledge of culinary techniques and terminology Demonstrates excellent guest service skills and an ability to give appropriate service recovery. NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Actively participates in meetings. Supervised by : Director of Hospitality & Food Service Education/Experience : High School Diploma; experience in prep and service. Language Ability: Ability to read and interpret documents such as manuals and write routine reports.  Ability to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form, ability to speak effectively before groups of customers or employees of organization. Physical Demands and Work Environment: The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include ability to adjust focus. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; use hands to finger, handle, or feel and talk and/or hear. The employee is frequently required to walk and reach with hands and arms. The employee is occasionally required to sit.  The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate to high. Regular and predictable attendance is required. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a1a0f425da01a1186421e53490": {
      "title": "Sous Chef",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Sous Chef Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 228 # of Openings: 0 SOUS CHEF SUMMARY OF BASIC JOB FUNCTION: The primary function of the Sous Chef is to assist in the preparation and operation of campus food services in relation to the Johnson Center, culinary/hospitality classes, student dining, all Cleary University internal and external public events on the Cleary University campuses. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : Consistently reports for duty on time, in uniform and offers professional, engaging and friendly service referring to cleaning schedules and performing the necessary duties. Prepares foods to the specifications, portions, arrangements and garnishes set forth by supervisor. Cooks menu items by following food handler safety codes and preparation procedures of the facility. Includes measuring, seasoning, knife work and working with kitchen equipment. Makes adjustments to food items to accommodate guests with allergies or specific dietary concerns. Assists during the service of functions and provides excellent customer service to all clients, students, staff and faculty on campus. Acts as liaison to front-of-house employees to ensure proper food service temperature Other duties as assigned. NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Assist Food & Beverage management team with receiving and storing product as requested. Assist in transporting of food, beverage and other items to and from campus buildings. Assist kitchen team in replenishing food items, crockery, cutlery, etc., on special functions/busy periods. Attend Department meetings as requested. Performs office, cleaning, FOH and other duties as assigned by supervisor. SUPERVISES: May occasionally assist student workers or Cleary kitchen staff in the completion of duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with Cleary University’s policies, procedures and applicable laws. Responsibilities include: interviewing, hiring and training employees; planning, assigning and directing work; appraising performance; rewarding and coaching employees; addressing complaints and resolving problems. Education/Experience: High School Diploma necessary; Culinary degree preferred or 3 years professional experience and at least two years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Language Ability: Ability to read and interpret documents such as manuals and write routine reports. Ability to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form, ability to speak effectively before groups of customers or employees of organization. Computer Skills: To perform this job successfully, an individual should have working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel and research Internet software. Physical Demands and Work Environment: The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 35 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include ability to adjust focus. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; use hands to finger, handle, or feel and talk and/or hear. The employee is frequently required to walk and reach with hands and arms. The employee is occasionally required to sit. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate to high. Regular and predictable attendance is required. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78839f9fd3ba8701a033aeb2456c13": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Clancy's Cashier",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker - Clancy's Cashier Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 220 # of Openings: 0 Clancy's Student Worker Cashier JOB SUMMARY: The Student Employee will support the daily operations of the Clancy's Café. This role provides hands-on experience in hospitality & food service while promoting a positive environment for Cleary University Clancy's team. The cashier will scan meal cards into the point-of-sale system from students who have purchased the meal plan to record their visit. The cashier will also ring up all non-meal plan customers using the Squares terminal. There are no cash handling responsibilities since all transactions are by credit card or house account. Cashier's are eligible to receive one complimentary meal per shift. Available shifts are: Breakfast= 8am-9:30am Lunch= 11:30am-1:30pm Dinner 5pm-7pm Saturday Brunch= 11am-1pm QUALIFICATIONS: Current Cleary University in good academic standing Interest in business administration, finance,  corporate accounting or related fields Excellent communication and teamwork skills Ability to work evenings, weekends, and flexible hours based on event schedules Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78859fa133542101a13ba499c32f54": {
      "title": "Janitorial Staff",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Janitorial Staff Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 231 # of Openings: 0 Janitorial Staff Cleary University | Howell, MI | Full-Time Cleary University is looking for a dependable, hard-working Housekeeper to help keep our campus clean, welcoming, and running smoothly. From student housing to classrooms to event spaces, you'll be part of what makes Cleary feel like home for our students, staff, and visitors. What we offer Day shift schedule Generous paid time off and paid holidays Medical, dental, and vision insurance Life insurance Retirement plan with a 5% employer match Tuition discount A stable job at a growing university What You'll Do Keep restrooms, offices, classrooms, and common areas clean and well-maintained Respond promptly and courteously to requests from staff, students, and guests Flag maintenance, safety, or supply needs to the right people Set up and break down rooms for meetings and events Pitch in on other duties as they come up What You'll Need High school diploma or G.E.D. Ability to keep up with the physical demands of an active role, including lifting up to 50 lbs. and regularly standing, walking, and moving throughout the day Willingness to work weekends, holidays, and off-hour shifts, indoors and outdoors in all weather when necessary A plus: previous custodial experience. What We're Looking For Someone who takes pride in their work and shares our commitment to Cleary University's mission, values, and student success. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome and encourage applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a1a0f425da01a11866c217350a": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Maintenance Technician Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 229 # of Openings: 0 Maintenance Tech Join a growing university and keep our campus running. Cleary is growing, and our facilities team is at the heart of it. You’ll handle hands-on repairs and upkeep across residence halls, classrooms, offices, athletic facilities and event spaces. If you like hands-on work, a mix of tasks, and seeing the difference you make everyday, this is the role for you! What we offer Day shift schedule Generous paid time off and paid holidays Medical, dental, and vision insurance Life insurance Retirement plan with a 5% employer match Tuition discount A stable job at a growing university What you’ll do Perform repairs and maintenance, including electrical, plumbing, carpentry, painting, drywall, and heating and cooling Respond to work requests from students, faculty, and staff, and get issues resolved quickly Maintain campus grounds and athletic facilities Manage waste removal and recycling Move furniture, equipment, and supplies around campus Respond to alarms and help keep campus secure Support students, faculty, and staff with timely, friendly service What you bring High school diploma or GED Ability to handle the physical demands of an active job and work indoors and outdoors in all weather Willingness to work some weekends, holidays, and off-hour shifts when campus needs require it Construction or custodial experience is a plus, but not required Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome and encourage applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, nation origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78859e9fd3bb25019fd7e3f4b414e7": {
      "title": "Student Worker: Museum Assistant",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker: Museum Assistant Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 217 # of Openings: 0 Museum Assistant: Arthur Secunda Museum Duties Under the direction of the Curator, the Museum Assistant will work on museum collections and programs: Collections Conduct collections inventory, checking work against collections management system (CMS) database Update object locations in CMS Assist with artifact handling, moving, and hanging Insert acid-free tissue as interleaving in flat file drawers Assist with cataloguing Cleary history material Rehouse Arthur Secunda and Cleary history archival material in acid-free folders and boxes Develop inventories of archival material Dismantle Cleary history shadowboxes to preserve historic documents Programs Assist with museum programs by facilitating art activities and giving museum information at events such including Secunda Second Sunday, High School Immersive Experience, Cleary Days, Night at the Museum, and offsite partner events Develop programs and program activities as needed Complete other duties as assigned related to museum exhibits and other projects Skills Artifact handling Museum registration and collections management basics Museum education best practices Program and event development Nonprofit cultural organization administration basics Requirements Must be a Cleary University Student Must be available to work at Secunda Museum events Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7883aca13c11d501a145d27b000d13": {
      "title": "Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Chief Financial Officer Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 232 # of Openings: 0 Chief Financial Officer Howell, Michigan  |  Full-Time | Exempt Cleary University seeks a strategic and entrepreneurial Chief Financial Officer (CFO) to guide the financial strategy of a growing and rapidly evolving private university based in Detroit and Howell, Michigan. In recent years, Cleary has strengthened its financial foundation, doubled enrollment, and developed a distinctive reputation for accelerated degree pathways serving working adults. These offerings have generated thousands of incremental enrollments with a 78% retention rate and a strong job placement rate, reflecting the strength of Cleary’s workforce-aligned model and its growing regional reputation. Reporting directly to President Alan Drimmer and serving as a key member of the executive leadership team, the CFO will work closely with the President to guide financial strategy, strengthen institutional planning and investments in financial systems, and support the university’s continued growth and innovation. The successful candidate will join a nimble leadership team and help build the financial frameworks needed to support program expansion, national initiatives, and new strategic ventures, while ensuring that financial strategy remains closely aligned with Cleary’s mission of preparing career-ready graduates. Cleary enters this search during a period of continued strategic investment and institutional progress. The University generates approximately $35 million in tuition revenue and is advancing a set of mission-aligned initiatives designed to expand access, improve outcomes, and strengthen its financial position, including: National expansion of Cleary’s accelerated programs in several major metropolitan cities and consideration of a for-profit entity to support growth Development of new schools and academic programs aligned with labor market trends Rollout of an innovative career development pathway model New philanthropy initiatives, including the development of a capital campaign Expansion of campus footprint These initiatives reflect the university’s commitment to disciplined growth and long-term financial strength. The University's newly adopted strategic plan, The Fourth Wave , presents an opportunity for the CFO to lead financial transformation within a high-growth education model. As the institution scales its nationally expanding adult and online programs – already demonstrating strong revenue generation and retention – while reinvesting in a vibrant residential campus, the CFO will shape a dynamic financial architecture that balances growth, margin, and mission. This role offers the chance to build sophisticated segment-level economics, optimize pricing and discount strategies across diverse student populations, and deploy capital in ways that directly fuel enrollment growth, program innovation, and long-term financial sustainability. The successful candidate will be a collaborative, hands-on financial leader who brings both strategic perspective and strong operational capability. The CFO will serve as a trusted partner to the President and senior leadership team, thrive in a lean and entrepreneurial environment, and share Cleary’s commitment to practical, career-focused education for working adults and diverse student populations. This is an on-site position with the flexibility to be based at either Cleary University's main campus in Howell or its Detroit office at the Jefferson Hub (JHub). Reporting directly to the President, the CFO oversees Budget, Accounting, Student Business Office, and Payroll. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The Chief Financial Officer oversees all university budgeting, accounting, financial analysis, and financial reporting functions and ensures that the university’s financial statements adhere to generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), working closely with external auditors. The CFO also oversees tax reporting and ensures that university operations comply with Internal Revenue Service (IRS) regulations and applicable State of Michigan requirements. In addition, the CFO develops and implements policies, standards, and procedures related to the university’s financial operations and ensures appropriate legal and regulatory compliance. Candidates for the CFO position will also be expected to: Serve as a strategic partner to the President and executive leadership team in aligning financial planning with institutional priorities, program innovation, and long-term growth initiatives Develop and monitor financial models, analyses, and interpretation of statistical and accounting information to assess operating results Oversee the University’s system of accounts and records on all University transactions and assets Coordinate and direct the preparation of the budget and financial forecasts Establish major financial objectives and policies for the institution and prepare reports that outline the University’s financial position in the areas of income, expenses and earnings based on past, present and future operations Collaborate with advancement leadership to support evolving philanthropic efforts and ensure strong financial infrastructure for future fundraising initiatives KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of university administration and the principles and practices of financial management Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and complex tasks simultaneously Experience with automated accounting systems and financial reporting tools Ability to build effective working relationships with diverse stakeholders across the university Demonstrated leadership ability, including supervising staff, delegating responsibilities, and fostering a collaborative team environment Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain a high level of confidentiality, and uphold institutional policies and priorities Demonstrated ability to connect financial strategy with institutional mission and student outcomes MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in finance, business, accounting, or a related field Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience in accounting or financial management in progressively responsible positions within a higher education institution; Or Five (5) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in financial planning, budgeting, and financial operations PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in finance, business, accounting, or a related field CPA certification About the Institution Cleary University is a private institution founded in 1883 with a long-standing commitment to innovation, applied learning, and entrepreneurship in business education. The University offers associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degree programs designed to prepare students for immediate and sustained success in a rapidly evolving workforce. Cleary's main campus is located in Howell, Michigan, with a growing presence in Detroit through its education center and offices at the Jefferson Hub (JHub). Together, these locations position the University to serve distinct student populations, develop regional partnerships, and engage with the broader Southeast Michigan business community. At the core of the academic experience is The Cleary Mind ™ , a distinctive, data-informed curricular framework focused on developing eight attributes most valued by employers: critical thinking, problem solving, ethics, creative thinking, communication, persuasion, entrepreneurship, and leadership. Fully integrated across the curriculum and co-curricular experience, The Cleary Mind™ reflects Cleary’s commitment to aligning academic programs with workforce needs and ensuring graduates are prepared to succeed and lead in dynamic organizational environments. Cleary serves a vibrant, career-focused student population, including traditional undergraduates as well as working professionals pursuing hybrid and fully online programs. Traditional undergraduate students may live in university residence halls, off-campus housing, or commute from home. The University’s emphasis on small class sizes, personalized support, and strong industry alignment fosters meaningful student engagement and career readiness. Cleary’s athletic teams, known as the Cougars, are an integral part of campus life, competing at the NAIA level as a member of the Wolverine-Hoosier Athletic Conference. Learn more about Cleary University at www.cleary.edu . Living in the Area With locations in Howell and Detroit, Cleary University offers access to two distinct communities within Southeast Michigan, providing a wide range of residential, professional, and recreational opportunities. Whether drawn to the charm of a smaller community or the energy of a major metropolitan area, candidates will find diverse options for living and working in the region. Cleary's main campus is in Howell, Michigan, part of Livingston County, one of the fastest-growing regions in Southeast Michigan. Situated between Detroit and Lansing and within easy driving distance of Ann Arbor, Howell offers highly regarded schools, family-friendly neighborhoods, abundant outdoor recreation, and a revitalized historic downtown with restaurants, arts venues, and year-round events. The area combines small-town character and natural beauty with convenient access to major employers, educational institutions, and regional transportation. Cleary's Detroit office is located at the Jefferson Hub (JHub) in Midtown, providing a professional workspace in the heart of Detroit's business, educational, and entrepreneurial community. Detroit offers a vibrant urban lifestyle with nationally recognized cultural institutions, professional sports, diverse residential neighborhoods, and a thriving restaurant and entertainment scene. The broader metropolitan area offers a wide range of suburban and urban living options, along with access to major employers, universities, and an extensive professional network. Learn more about the region at www.livgov.com and www.visitdetroit.com. To Apply To be considered, you must apply directly at: https://acesrch.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a21esjy30qw5 Applications will be reviewed as they are received and should include a cover letter and curriculum vita. Ideally cover letters should not exceed two pages. All applications are treated confidentially. Inquiries, referrals, and nominations are also treated confidentially. Inquiries and questions : Please send to ClearyCFO@acesrch.com Nominations and referrals : Please send the nominee’s name, title, and contact information if available to nominations@acesrch.com Institutional Information Cleary University is committed to being a workplace that is not only free of discrimination, but one that genuinely fosters inclusion and belonging. Cleary strongly believes that workforce diversity creates an environment in which its employees can thrive. Cleary understands and embraces the variety through which people gain experiences whether through professional, personal, educational, or volunteer opportunities. Cleary University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7883aca13c11d501a145e07a3d1324": {
      "title": "Manager of Advancement Operations & Engagement",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Manager of Advancement Operations & Engagement Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 233 # of Openings: 0 Manager of Advancement Operations & Engagement Cleary University | Howell, Michigan | Full-Time Be the engine behind a growing university’s fundraising. Cleary University is a fast-growing, student-centered institution in southeast Michigan. As Manager of Advancement Operations & Engagement, you’ll be the person who makes our fundraising work, combining database expertise with donor and alumni relationships. You’ll report directly to the Vice President of Advancement and work closely with campus partners, and your work will directly support student scholarships and the university’s growth. If you like organized systems, good stories, and seeing your work turn into real support for students, this role is for you. Why Work at Cleary? Generous paid time off and paid holidays Medical, dental, and vision insurance Life insurance Retirement plan with a 5% employer match Tuition discount Hybrid flexibility, as approved A chance to take on a wide-ranging role at a university on the rise What you’ll do Run advancement operations Own our donor database: keep records clean, standardize profiles, and run regular data audits Oversee gift processing, pledge tracking, tax receipts, and acknowledgment letters, and reconcile gifts with the Finance Office Build custom queries, reports, mailing lists, and dashboards that help the team make decisions Manage the grant calendar, including deadlines, reporting schedules, attachments, and post-award requirements Gather student stories and scholarship data to create impact reports for donors Drive engagement and annual giving Coordinate annual giving, including direct mail, digital campaigns, and giving days Research corporate and foundation funders and help prepare proposals, budgets, and application materials Partner with Marketing on alumni engagement and donor stewardship, including events, newsletters, and impact updates Keep the stewardship calendar on track so donors hear from us consistently Talk with alumni and donors to capture their stories for publications, campaign materials, and grant proposals Pitch in on special projects that support our fundraising priorities What you bring Bachelor’s degree 3 to 5 years of experience in advancement, annual giving, business operations, data management, project coordination, higher education, marketing, or a related field Comfort with databases and CRMs (DonorPerfect, Salesforce, or similar), Excel or Google Sheets, and digital communication tools Strong organization, attention to detail, and follow-through Clear writing and speaking, and a knack for building relationships Experience managing timelines, calendars, and multiple workflows at once Discretion with confidential donor, gift, and scholarship information Nice to have Experience in higher education, especially scholarship administration, alumni relations, or working across departments Experience with giving days, direct mail or digital campaigns, or corporate and foundation grant proposals Experience building custom reports and dashboards Where you’ll work This position is based at our Howell, Michigan campus. Hybrid work is available as approved, and you may occasionally attend regional events. Equal opportunity employer Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. We provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. If you need an accommodation during the application process, please contact Human Resources. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78879ea15447f701a1606b05d1336d": {
      "title": "Admissions Advisor",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Admissions Advisor Location: Detroit Job Id: 236 # of Openings: 0 Admissions Advisor Help the people who protect our communities earn their degrees. Cleary University is a growing, student-centered university in southeast Michigan, and our Adult Accelerated programs are built for working adults. As a Public Safety Admissions Advisor, you’ll guide law enforcement officers, firefighters, EMTs, corrections staff, and other public safety professionals from their first question to their first day of class. You’ll own the whole relationship: reaching out, listening to a student’s goals, working through concerns like cost, time, and transfer credit, and helping them take each step. You’ll work toward clear enrollment goals, and you’ll see the results of your work in the students who start. Why work at Cleary? Generous paid time off and paid holidays Medical, dental, and vision insurance Life insurance Retirement plan with a 5% employer match Tuition discount A role with real ownership at a growing university What you’ll do Recruit and enroll Adult Accelerated and Public Safety students through phone, text, email, virtual meetings, and in-person visits Own your pipeline of prospective students, from first inquiry through application, enrollment, registration, and start Learn each student’s career and education goals, and help them work through barriers like cost, schedules, transfer credit, and tuition reimbursement Explain Cleary’s programs and the benefits of accelerated study for working adults Keep students moving with clear next steps and deadlines, and follow up consistently Reconnect with past inquiries, incomplete applicants, and inactive leads Lead information sessions, presentations, and one-on-one advising appointments Represent Cleary at police and fire departments, correctional facilities, public safety agencies, employer sites, and community events Work with Enrollment Leadership to spot barriers and improve the student experience Use Salesforce, ZoomInfo, and Microsoft Teams to manage your outreach and track your results What you bring Bachelor’s degree Experience in admissions, recruitment, sales, business development, outreach, or another goal-driven, relationship-based role A track record of building relationships, managing a pipeline, following up, and meeting goals Strong phone and interpersonal skills, and an easy way of connecting with working adults and public safety professionals Comfort with CRM systems (Salesforce preferred), ZoomInfo, and Microsoft Teams Strong organization and attention to detail, with the ability to juggle priorities and a large pipeline Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced setting Availability for occasional evenings, weekends, and regional travel Nice to have 3 or more years in admissions, recruitment, sales, or business development Higher education admissions experience, especially meeting or exceeding enrollment goals Experience with adult, non-traditional, or accelerated students Experience working with law enforcement, fire, EMS, corrections, or government Background in employer partnerships or workforce development Familiarity with Prior Learning Assessment, transfer credit, and tuition reimbursement Who thrives here You’re motivated, persistent, and resilient. You build rapport quickly, you’re comfortable being measured on your results, and you care about students as much as you care about enrollment numbers. The physical side of the job You’ll spend much of your time sitting, talking, and using technology. You’ll need to lift up to 10 pounds. This is an onsite role with occasional evening and weekend work and local and regional travel. Equal opportunity employer Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. We provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78859fa152cc4201a15b29ba0d6f47": {
      "title": "Campus Dining & Event Services Cashier",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Campus Dining & Event Services Cashier Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 235 # of Openings: 0 Campus Dining & Event Services Cashier SUMMARY: The Campus Dining & Event Services Assistant/Cashier plays an important role in creating a warm, welcoming, and high-quality dining experience for Cleary University students, employees, and guests. This part-time position offers an afternoon schedule and the unique option to take summers off — perfect for someone looking for flexibility and a positive, community-oriented work environment. In this role, you’ll support daily operations at Clancy’s Café (student dining) and assist with Cleary University events — from campus gatherings to community celebrations — ensuring every guest enjoys great service and a friendly atmosphere. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Set up the student dining room and event spaces, ensuring hospitality and service standards are met or exceeded. Ensure all areas are clean, organized, and maintained to high cleanliness standards throughout shifts. Assist with opening and closing duties, including storing reusable goods, cleaning equipment, and organizing spaces. Act as a liaison with kitchen staff to maintain proper food service temperatures and replenish food items as needed during events. Adhere to health, safety, and university regulations. Perform other duties as assigned. BENEFITS OF THE ROLE: Afternoon shifts that support a healthy work-life balance. Summers off if desired, offering additional flexibility. A dynamic and collaborative work environment with opportunities for growth. Paid sick time off. Retirement plan Free or significantly discounted tuition for employees and their dependents at Cleary University and hundreds of other institutions nationwide. QUALIFICATIONS: High School Diploma required; two years of experience in food service operations preferred. Must be available afternoons and early evenings, until 8pm. Ability to communicate effectively and follow written and verbal instructions. Physical ability to lift and move up to 35 pounds and work in a moderately noisy environment. Cleary University is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment where all individuals feel a sense of belonging. We encourage applications from all qualified individuals and are an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    }
  },
